@startuml propagation-sequence
title Future subsystem scenario — one log at the handler, panic stays off the logger

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "main" as Main
participant "level" as Level
participant "asset" as Asset
participant "io" as Io
participant "render" as Render
participant "logging" as Log

note over Main
  Illustrative. io, asset, render, and level
  are not in the tree yet. The rules are
  ADR-005 and ADR-007.
end note

== Recoverable NotFound — the level handles it ==

Main -> Level : loadWall("missing.png")
Level -> Asset : loadTexture("missing.png")
Asset -> Io : readFile("assets/missing.png")
Io --> Asset : unexpected NotFound\nmessage holds errno\nno log
Asset --> Level : unexpected wrap(Asset NotFound)\nno log
Level -> Log : warning(Category::Asset,\n"using placeholder: {}", error)
note right of Log
  One record. The formatter renders
  the asset frame and the io cause.
end note
Level --> Main : success, placeholder texture

== Unrecoverable environment failure — main handles it ==

Main -> Level : loadWall("present.png")
Level -> Asset : loadTexture("present.png")
Asset --> Level : texture
Level -> Render : upload(texture)
Render --> Level : unexpected DeviceLost\nnative code in the message\nno log
Level --> Main : unexpected withContext("uploading wall")\nno log
Main -> Log : fatal(Category::Core,\n"level load failed: {}", error)
Main -> Log : flush()
Main -> Main : shut down initialized systems
Main --> Main : return non-zero

== Panic — logger is not a participant ==

participant "caller" as Caller
participant "panic" as Panic
participant "stderr" as Err

Caller -> Panic : invariant or bad_alloc
Panic -> Panic : format into a 1024-byte stack buffer\nor a fixed literal if formatting throws
Panic -> Err : descriptor write
Panic -> Panic : abort()
note over Log
  panic() does not call logging,\nflush, or a running-state query.
  This still holds when initialize()\nhas never been called.
end note

@enduml
